record; \code{niche_kept}: the share of the bins occupied by all records
that are still occupied.
\item \code{null_coverage}: the same coverage for random subsets of the same size
(\code{n_null} draws), and \code{coverage_gain} = \code{env_coverage} -
\code{null_coverage}: does the thinning keep more of the environment than
losing the same number of records at random?
\item \code{nn_km}, \code{clark_evans}: mean nearest-neighbour distance and its ratio
